      "reference": "11.11",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "πῶς οὖν ἐτάσωμεν τῷ εἰς τὴν ὑμετέραν κακῷ ἐνδομυχοῦντι",
          "english_quote": "How, then, are we to deal with the evil lurking within you",
          "issue": "'Deal with' is too general to make the examination, testing, or questioning force of ἐτάσωμεν visible. No lexical decision explains this broadening. The confirmed printed construction should not be treated as an OCR error merely because its dative complement is unfamiliar.",
          "suggested_revision": "Compare a source-transparent candidate such as 'How, then, are we to examine the evil lurking within you ...?' Preserve the verb's examination or questioning force, and document the interpretation of its dative complement. The complete revised sentence requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "διαλλάγητε ἑαυτοῖς·",
          "english_quote": "Be reconciled with yourselves:",
          "issue": "The reflexive interpretation is defensible in the context of an internal struggle, but plural ἑαυτοῖς also permits the materially different reciprocal rendering 'with one another'. Neither that alternative nor the reason for choosing self-reconciliation is disclosed.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note preserving 'Be reconciled with one another' as an alternative and explaining that the main text chooses 'with yourselves' because the surrounding argument concerns evil and irrational desire within the hearers. Do not describe either interpretation as uniquely established.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἔχθρα τις ἐστὶν θεῷ ἐν ὑμῖν ἄλογος ἐπιθυμία·",
          "english_quote": "There is within you an irrational desire hostile to God;",
          "issue": "The supplied ἔχθρα is the noun 'enmity', qualified by τις, not the adjective ἐχθρά, 'hostile'. The draft replaces the classification of irrational desire as a kind of enmity with an existential statement about a hostile desire, obscuring the nominal assertion.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use 'Irrational desire within you is a kind of enmity toward God;' or another rendering that explicitly preserves the noun and its qualification.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
